# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# KaamBill: environment variables (TEMPLATE, no real secrets)
#
# The app starts WITHOUT a .env file and without any key. Without GROQ_API_KEY every screen works, and
# building a bill shows a "Groq key not set" message.
#
# Local dev:   cp .env.example .env   (at the repo root; git-ignored), then set GROQ_API_KEY.
# Docker:      docker compose up --build   (reads GROQ_API_KEY from this .env if it exists)
# Production:  set the SERVER variables on your host (Render: Environment tab).
#
#   SERVER  (no prefix)  → only readable by the /api functions. Secrets go HERE.
#   CLIENT  (VITE_ ...)  → bundled into the browser app and visible to anyone.
#                          NEVER put an API key in a VITE_ variable.
#
# Not needed at all: Wispr Flow (a dictation app the user signs in to; it types into
# KaamBill's text box like a keyboard, no key), and no text-to-speech service (the app never speaks).
# See docs/architecture.md §13 for what each service is used for.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ═════════════════════════ NEEDED TO BUILD BILLS (the app starts without it) ══════

# Groq: bill extraction (/api/extract). Only text is sent to Groq, never audio.
# Get a free key at https://console.groq.com/keys. Leave empty to see the "key not set" message.
GROQ_API_KEY=


# ═════════════════════════ OPTIONAL (defaults shown; uncomment to change) ═══════

# --- Server: LLM extraction ---------------------------------------------------
# LLM_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b
# LLM_FALLBACK_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-20b      # used once after a 429 or timeout
# LLM_REASONING_EFFORT=low                   # low | medium | high
# LLM_MAX_TOKENS=640                         # counts against Groq's tokens-per-minute limit
# EXTRACT_TIMEOUT_MS=6000

# --- Server: abuse and cost protection (set these in PRODUCTION) ----------------
# Allowed origins (CORS + Origin check). Default allows http://localhost:5173 and the server's own
# address (same origin, e.g. http://localhost:3000 in Docker), so you rarely need to set this.
# On Render the service URL (RENDER_EXTERNAL_URL) is added automatically; list custom domains here.
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://kaambillapp.onrender.com
# RATE_LIMIT_PER_MIN=30
# Persistent rate-limit store (in-memory limits don't hold across serverless instances):
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=

# --- Server: logging (logs never contain customer phone numbers) ---------------------
# LOG_LEVEL=info                             # debug | info | warn | error

# --- Client: the mic (the green mic button uses the browser's speech recognition; Wispr Flow needs nothing here) --------
# VITE_VAD_SILENCE_MS=4000                   # pause (ms) allowed between words before the turn ends

# --- Client: confidence thresholds (architecture.md §5.5) ---------------------------
# VITE_CONF_HIGH=0.85
# VITE_CONF_LOW=0.6

# --- Client: usage tracking without personal data (PostHog key is public by design) ---
# VITE_POSTHOG_KEY=
# VITE_POSTHOG_HOST=https://app.posthog.com

# --- Client: demo mode (pre-loads the canonical demo data for judges; or use ?demo=1) --
# VITE_DEMO_MODE=true

# --- Client: API base URL (same origin on Vercel) -----------------------------------
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api
